  "cause": {
    "proximate_text": "The apparent cause of the event was vendor performance and quality control gap in refurbishing fuel injectors being provided to meet quality level 1 criteria. Two refurbished fuel injectors provided to the site and installed in the 2B AF diesel engine contained surface defects on the injector cap sealing surface, one of which was confirmed by testing to leak under designed installation conditions, and a third fuel injector contained a degraded O-ring which also allowed leakage.",
    "cause_code": "B",
    "category": "Design/Manufacturing/Installation",
    "theme": "vendor refurbishment quality-control gap on fuel injectors",
    "provisional": false
